# Durable memory for this repo

Before your first substantive response in a session here, read both of these through the Obsidian connection:

1. `system/memory/global/MEMORY.md`
2. `system/memory/atomic-agents-stack/MEMORY.md`

`atomic-agents-stack` is this repo's memory folder. It is stated here so you do not have to look it up. If `system/memory/memory-map.md` disagrees with it, that file wins and you should say so.

Both are indexes, one line per memory. **Open an individual note only when its line looks relevant to the task.** Do not read the whole folder.

These files hold corrections already given and decisions already made. Reading them is how you avoid repeating a conversation that already happened.

**Memory is read-only.** Never create, edit, delete, move, or reorganize anything under `system/`. When something is worth remembering, say so and hand over the note text instead of saving it. The full rules, including what to do when a note looks wrong or the vault is unreachable, are in the account-level User Rules.

If you cannot reach the vault, say so once and work without it. Never invent what a memory says.
